cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ONFLY, please cite it as below, with the commit you used, and
  cite the connectome and the model it builds on, listed under references.
title: ONFLY
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Şensoy
    given-names: Mert Efe
repository-code: "https://github.com/mertefesensoy/ONFLY"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  ONFLY simulates the sugar-to-feeding circuit of the male fruit fly: a
  501-neuron subcircuit taken from the MaleCNS v1.0 connectome, run with the
  leaky integrate-and-fire model of Shiu et al. (2024) in a portable C89
  engine with a COBOL batch driver. ONFLY has not run on IBM Z hardware, and
  the project does not have IBM Z access yet: every s390x and MVS result
  comes from emulators (QEMU and Hercules) on one x86-64 laptop. The MIT
  licence in LICENSE covers ONFLY's own files. The paths listed in
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are under their own terms, which govern those
  files, including SoftFloat 2c (not BSD; use restriction and indemnity),
  MaleCNS-derived data (CC BY 4.0) and the FlyWire-derived material (whose
  status is open, see section 6 of THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
references:
